profile.comment=Ultra Performance (default) / Balanced / Visual Performance. Pick the preset that fits your PC, then fine tune below.

screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
screen.LIGHTING=Lighting and Colour
screen.ATMOSPHERE=Atmosphere
screen.VEGETATION=Vegetation
screen.WATER=Water
screen.SHADOWS=Shadows
screen.POST=Post Processing

option.POST_PROCESSING=Post Processing Pass
option.POST_PROCESSING.comment=The full-screen pass that draws distance fog, the colour grade and the underwater tint. Turning it off removes an entire pass: terrain lighting, sky and water still look better than vanilla, but fog and grading are gone. The second biggest FPS lever after shadows.

option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How many blocks the shadow pass covers. Lower means much less geometry re-rendered per frame. Shadows fade out instead of stopping at a hard line.

option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Grass, flowers, crops and leaves sway in the wind. Costs two sine calls per vertex and nothing per pixel, so it is on even in the fastest preset.

option.WAVING_WATER=Waving Water
option.WAVING_WATER.comment=The water surface moves up and down slightly. Vertex cost only.

option.WAVE_STRENGTH=Wave Strength
option.WAVE_STRENGTH.comment=How far vegetation and water travel. Does not change the cost.

option.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS=Underwater Caustics
option.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS.comment=Animated light ripples on everything while the camera is underwater. Free above water, two sine calls below it.

option.HANDHELD_LIGHT=Handheld Light
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT.comment=A torch or lantern in your hand lights the ground around you, which is what makes a torch useful while mining. Carrying nothing costs one comparison.

option.DIMENSION_TUNING=Dimension Tuning
option.DIMENSION_TUNING.comment=Warm the light and thicken the fog in the Nether, cool the light and clear the fog in the End.

option.shadowIntervalSize=Shadow Interval
option.shadowIntervalSize.comment=Higher values soften the banding that a 1024 shadow map shows on long shadows.

option.entityShadowDistanceMul=Entity Shadow Distance
option.entityShadowDistanceMul.comment=How far away entities still cast shadows, as a fraction of the shadow distance. Lower means much less entity geometry in the shadow pass.

option.SHADOW_QUALITY=Shadow Quality
option.SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=Off skips the shadow pass completely, which is the single biggest win on integrated graphics. Hard is one tap per pixel, Soft averages four.
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.0=Off
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.1=Hard
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.2=Soft

option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Lower is faster and blurrier. 1024 is the recommended low-end value.

option.SHADOW_STRENGTH=Shadow Strength
option.SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How much direct sunlight the shadows remove. They only apply where sky light reaches, so interiors and caves are unaffected.

option.EXPOSURE=Brightness
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Overall brightness multiplier, applied after lighting.

option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.SATURATION.comment=Colour saturation around the brightness of each pixel.

option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.CONTRAST.comment=Contrast around mid grey.

option.SUNSET_STRENGTH=Sunset Warmth
option.SUNSET_STRENGTH.comment=How warm sunrise and sunset colours are, in the sky, the fog and the light tint.

option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Night Brightness
option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Light level of moonlit and unlit areas after dark.

option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Higher pulls the distance fog closer, lower pushes it away.

option.CLOUD_SHADING=Cloud Shading
option.CLOUD_SHADING.comment=Grades vanilla's cloud shapes by time of day: white by day, blue-grey at night, warm underneath at sunrise and sunset. Costs a handful of arithmetic on cloud pixels only.

option.SKY_CIRRUS=High Cirrus
option.SKY_CIRRUS.comment=Thin high cloud streaks over the sky, sliding as you move. Four sine calls on sky pixels only.

option.SUN_GLARE=Sun Glare
option.SUN_GLARE.comment=Warm glare around the sun's position on screen, strongest at sunrise and sunset. Only drawn over clean sky, so it never haloes a mountain.

option.VEGETATION_POLISH=Vegetation Polish
option.VEGETATION_POLISH.comment=Grass and leaves get richer colour and a little extra light, as if the sun went through them.

option.WATER_DEPTH=Water Depth
option.WATER_DEPTH.comment=Water colour and transparency follow how deep it is: shallow water stays clear, deep water turns blue, and shallows get a bright shoreline rim. One depth fetch.

option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Sky colour reflected on water, weighted by viewing angle. Arithmetic only, no extra texture fetches.

option.WATER_REFLECTION_STRENGTH=Reflection Strength
option.WATER_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the sky is mixed into the water surface.

option.WATER_WAVES=Water Waves
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=Animated shimmer on the reflected direction. Adds four sin or cos per water pixel.

option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=Bright pass glow. Four extra fetches of the scene buffer at full resolution.

option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Darkens the corners of the screen.

option.SSAO=Ambient Occlusion
option.SSAO.comment=Depth only contact shadows in grooves and corners. Four extra depth fetches and five depth linearisations per pixel.
